 "notes": "CAPP-9T (IBS/CAPP) double-cell multiple-cell cavity haloscope. Curve extracted pixel-wise from Fig. 5 (eprint exclusion.png), main panel: g_agamma/g_KSVZ (linear axis, calibrated on y ticks 10-50 and x labels 13.0-13.8 ueV) vs mass. Paper quotes average exclusion g >= 11.1 x g_KSVZ at 90% CL over 13.0-13.9 ueV; extracted median ratio ~11.3, consistent. Converted with g_KSVZ(m) = 1.92*alpha/(2pi f_a), m_a = 5.7 ueV x (1e12 GeV/f_a), i.e. g_KSVZ = 3.91e-16 GeV^-1 x (m/ueV). Paper assumes rho_a = 0.45 GeV/cm^3 (canonical, no rescaling). Median per-bin values used, which smooths narrow removed-bin spikes; mode-mixing gap bins near 13.34 ueV skipped.",
